   "title": "Refund Manager: Handling Chargeback Notices and Invoice Discrepancies",
   "content_summary": "Guidance on resolving chargeback notices and invoice errors in Refund Manager, focusing on identifying operator errors or third-party service failures.",
   "content_body": "1. Verify the transaction ID in Refund Manager to determine if the charge was processed manually (operator error) or via an external API (third-party failure). 2. If manual, correct the invoice directly and issue a customer education note on the new billing cycle. 3. If automated, check the Chargeback Handler logs for API timeouts; if confirmed, apply the standard workaround of delaying the next billing cycle by 24 hours while the vendor investigates. 4. Always confirm the resolution with the customer before closing the ticket to prevent duplicate disputes."
